# netsurf: lift a fieldset's legend from its own border and padding (patch 228)
# Generated 2026-10-10
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser e71759b (patch stack through 227)
#
# Fixes a regression from patch 222, which lifted the legend onto the
# fieldset's top border with a fixed margin-top in default.css (the
# default 2px border plus 0.35em padding) on every <legend>. A fieldset
# reset to no border or padding -- Bootstrap's is -- then had its legend
# pulled 8-9px up over the content above, a legend outside a fieldset was
# lifted too, and a fieldset with another border or padding put its legend
# off the border.
#
#  - box_construct.c, box.h: VB_FIELDSET flags <fieldset> boxes.
#  - layout.c: vb_legend_margins() gives the rendered legend -- the
#    fieldset's first <legend> child, in flow (not floated or absolutely
#    positioned; a floated legend, as Bootstrap's, is an ordinary float, as
#    in browsers) -- a margin-top less the fieldset's top border + padding
#    and a margin-bottom plus its top padding, so its margin box starts at
#    the fieldset's border-box top and the content after it starts the
#    padding below it. Applied where block margins are resolved
#    (layout_block_find_dimensions) and where top margins are collapsed
#    (layout_next_margin_block), which re-reads them.
#  - default.css: the fixed legend margins go; only a fieldset's legend
#    is fit-content (a loose legend is a full-width block, as in browsers).
#
# Test: testpages/pages/HTML-legend-reset.html (LEGEND228, 4 checks,
# Chromium 4/4; with 222 alone, 0/4): Bootstrap's reset fieldset, a
# fieldset without border or padding, a legend outside a fieldset, and a
# 4px border / 10px padding fieldset. FIELDSET222 5/5 (its legend now at
# 0 rather than -1).
